# Build output
build/
build-*/
out/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# SwiftPM's own build output (src.swift/MediaViewerChrome), separate from
# cmake/darwin.cmake's build-*/ tree above -- `swift build` writes here when
# run directly against the package rather than through cmake's own
# --build-path (build-darwin/swift-chrome, already covered by build-*/).
.build/

# vcpkg manifest-mode install tree
vcpkg_installed/

# Frame-time harness artefacts. The report is per-run; the baseline is per-machine
# and is restored from CI cache rather than committed — a baseline captured on a
# noisy box lowers the bar for every later PR (plan/09).
frametime-report.json
frametime-idle-report.json
frametime-baseline.json

# The test corpus does not live in git (plan/09). Tens of GB of RAW, HEIC and 4K
# video, most of it not redistributable. A manifest of (url, sha256, licence)
# belongs here; the files do not.
corpus/
tests/corpus/

# MSVC / VS
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.pdb
*.idb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.aps

# .NET
*.nupkg
project.lock.json

# PR 5 test corpus — generated locally, never committed.
# plan/09: "Do not put the RAW corpus in git." Same rule for 4K video clips:
# they live in the repo so every session can reach them, and stay out of history.
#
# The GENERATOR is not corpus. Ignoring the whole directory took generate.sh
# with it, so a clean clone had no clips AND no way to make them, and every
# real-clip test skipped while ctest still reported success. Ignore the
# contents, keep the script. A directory-level ignore also stops git
# descending, so this has to be `dir/*` rather than `dir/` for the negation
# below to be reachable at all.
tools/testmedia/*
!tools/testmedia/generate.sh
# PR 7 RAW samples: the fetcher and its (url, sha256, licence) manifest are
# source; tools/testmedia/raw/ is not.
!tools/testmedia/fetch-raw.ps1
!tools/testmedia/raw-manifest.json
!tools/testmedia/fetch-heif.ps1
!tools/testmedia/heif-manifest.json
# PR 7: the seed generator. Its output (tests/data/seeds, tests/data/broken)
# is tiny, synthetic and licence-clean, so unlike the clips it IS committed.
!tools/testmedia/make-seeds.py

# libFuzzer output (PR 7). tools/fuzz/run.ps1 writes working corpora and
# artefacts under fuzz-out/ in the build tree; a harness run by hand drops
# crash-/leak-/timeout-/oom- files in the current directory. Reproducers worth
# keeping are copied into tests/data/broken/ on purpose.
fuzz-out/
crash-*
leak-*
timeout-*
oom-*
slow-unit-*

# Local harness output. `--av-soak --csv` and the frame-time gate both write
# reports next to wherever you ran them, and both keep getting picked up by a
# `git add -A`. They are measurements of one machine on one afternoon, not
# source: the numbers that matter go in the PR or the README, not in history.
scratch-av.csv
drift.csv
soak.json

# Scratch notes. Working files for a slice in progress, not the plan — the
# plan is plan/.
PR5UInotes.txt

.claude/
